On Mon, Oct 10, 2011 at 08:25:16AM -0700, Muhammad Nael wrote:
> This was a simple question... Where can one ask simple (as close
> to that) questions without opening a thread that says
> 'discussion'? I'm pretty sure much of what's in here only needs
> simple answers and sometimes booleans! So, where is this place?

A place where you can ask a question about the Shannon entropy of a
*language*, a concept that regularily generates scholarly research
papers, without generating a discussion?  I would very much hope
that no such place exists; that would be a sad and boring place.

In this particular case, no-one knows the answer because no-one has
studied it.  We're all unpaid volunteers.  Feel free to do it
yourself; http://corpus.lojban.org/ would be a good starting point.

-Robin

